1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,500
A firefly lights this lighthouse. And switches it off right on time.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,300
They rode the wrong way. The conductor punched one more hole. That makes it a transfer.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,900
This time it's the right way. Even the bird finally points forward.

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,500
A seaside station at sunset. The boat to the far south comes into this harbor.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,900
The boat comes at night. It follows the lighthouse beam.

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,700
The keeper is a firefly. The lens turns his tiny glow into a beam.

7
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,100
Now they only have to wait. The last fish skewer, half each.

8
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,700
But someone is waving from the rocks. It is not a hello.

9
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,300
A baby crab's claw is stuck in the rocks. The tide is coming in.

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,500
The rescue team sets out. The rocks are slippery.

11
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,900
Pulling doesn't work. The crab only pushes sideways.

12
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,500
The water rises and storm clouds roll in. The boat's hour is getting close.

13
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:33,100
They pushed on three, but the wave pushed first. The claw is free.

14
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,900
They go in for a thank-you hug and keep missing. Crabs only walk sideways.

15
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,300
So Mochi gave him a ride. The claw knows the way.

16
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,900
It is getting dark and the waves are high. The pebble lights their steps.

17
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,300
The crab family. They clap with their claws.

18
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,100
Mochi watched for a long while. The pebble in his backpack grew warm.

19
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,700
The gift is a conch shell. What it is for, nobody knows yet.

20
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,300
Back at the pier, one light on the horizon. The boat is coming.

21
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,900
Meanwhile, at the top of the lighthouse. The watch hand has reached the moon.

22
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,500
The keeper closes his logbook and packs his bag. Time to go home.

23
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,500
Click.

24
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:01,100
The lighthouse went dark. And the boat is still out at sea.

25
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,900
He means no harm. Leaving on time is simply his rule.

26
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,500
Mochi lifts his pebble. It is the only light they have.

27
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,500
The boat cannot find the harbor and turns away. The pebble is too small. (To be continued)

